d Ramaswamy's large financial edge keep this within reach for Republicans, so a narrow Democratic edge with wide uncertainty fits the evidence.", "watch": "Whether Ramaswamy's advertising advantage closes the gap in the final weeks, or the favorable national environment and economic concerns extend Acton's lead.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike DeWine (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's governor's race is competitive, with Democrat Amy Acton holding a modest lead over Republican Vivek Ramaswamy in an open seat created by Mike DeWine's term limit. Recent polls diverge: Republican-leaning surveys put Ramaswamy up a point, while Marist and Suffolk show Acton ahead by six to nine. Aggregated polling averages place Acton up roughly three to six points, and prediction markets price her chances around 58 to 62 percent.\n\nThe state's Republican lean and Ramaswamy's financial edge — he has raised about $25 million to Acton's $5 million and holds a four-to-one cash advantage — give Republicans a path. Most race raters still call the contest a Tossup, though the Silver Bulletin rates it Lean D. A Libertarian is also on the ballot. Economic concerns and a contrast over the candidates' wealth have featured in recent coverage as both campaign across the state, including on college campuses.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.662, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6672, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6954, "margin": 2.5}]}